# AZM Dev Bridge — feedback loop (mandatory)

Claude Desktop dispatches EasyCasa work via **azm-dev-bridge** (`send_dev_task` → `task_<hex>`). Claude **cannot** read this repo or GitHub PRs. If you finish work without updating the public status ledger, Claude will incorrectly report “still running, no PR”.

## When this applies
Any handoff that mentions: `azm-dev-bridge`, `send_dev_task`, `task_<hex>`, Kaizen `K EC …`, polish `PP-*` / `PK-*` / `V-*`, or “R&D FEEDBACK — for Claude”.

## Required status surface
Canonical poll file (Claude WebFetches after it lands on `main`):

`docs/azm-deliverables/_bridge/status-ledger.json`

Also write per-task:

`docs/azm-deliverables/<K-EC-x.y>/STATUS.json`

Use the helper (do not hand-edit unless the script is unavailable):

```bash
node scripts/azm-bridge-status.mjs upsert \
  --bridge task_<hex> \
  --kaizen "K EC x.y" \
  --polish PP-N \
  --lifecycle <dispatched|running|pr_open|pr_ready|merged|blocked|failed|cancelled> \
  --pr <number> --pr-state DRAFT|OPEN|MERGED \
  --agent-status IDLE|RUNNING|ERROR \
  --agent-bc bc-… \
  --agent-url https://cursor.com/agents/bc-… \
  --branch cursor/… \
  --summary "one line Claude can quote" \
  --next-action "what human/Claude should do next"
```

Then print the forwardable block into chat:

```bash
node scripts/azm-bridge-status.mjs claude-block --bridge task_<hex>
```

## Timing rules (do not skip)
1. **Start of work** → `lifecycle=running` (include `bridgeTaskId` if present in the brief).
2. **Immediately after the draft PR exists** → `lifecycle=pr_open` with `prUrl` / `prNumber` / `prState`. Commit + push the ledger update on the **same** feature branch (or a tiny follow-up commit) so Claude can see it once merged — and paste the `AZM_BRIDGE_STATUS` block in the chat progress update **now** (Aziz forwards to Claude even before merge).
3. **Ready for review** → `lifecycle=pr_ready` (mark draft ready only if asked).
4. **After merge** → `lifecycle=merged` on `main` (or a docs PR).
5. **Hard fail / cancel** → `lifecycle=failed|cancelled` with `errors[]`.

## Chat / PR contract
- Every progress update for a bridge task must include the `<!-- AZM_BRIDGE_STATUS_BEGIN --> … END -->` block from `claude-block`.
- Every bridge PR body must end with `## R&D FEEDBACK — for Claude` **and** the same status block near the top of that section.
- Update Kaizen (category + %) and Startup (phase + %) with the PR URL when the handoff asks for boards.

## Anti-patterns (caused the 2026-08-14 miss)
- Opening a PR then going IDLE without ledger/status block → Claude polls bridge and says “still running, no PR”.
- Relying only on Cursor agent IDLE / chat summary.
- Re-dispatching the same Kaizen code after a bridge timeout without `list_tasks` + ledger check.
